From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:51:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): "+ Create project" moves the row into the new
 project at once [daveey]

Follow-up to 05e04c066a (instant move-to-project). createProjectAndMoveSession
(Cmd-Shift-P "+ Create project") still waited for projects.list + mkdir +
projects.create + session.workspace.move + a 2-5 s tree refetch, because the
destination project was not in $projectTree yet, so the optimistic move had
no node to file the row under.

Now it reuses a same-named node when the tree has one, else inserts a
provisional node (id provisional:<name>) and files the row there before any
RPC. Tree payloads keep the provisional node until the backend lists a
project of that name, then retarget the pending move to the real node. A
failed create/move removes the node and restores the old owner.

renameProjectSessions moved to store/projects-rename-sessions.ts to offset
projects.ts growth under its line ratchet.

Tests: projects-move-optimistic.test.ts (row owned by the provisional node
while projects.create is pending, survives a stale refresh, ends on the real
node; failure removes the node and restores p_src). Both fail without the
change.
